      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the number of toothpicks at the 250th stage of the pattern.\n\nThe pattern starts with 4 toothpicks. In each of the subsequent stages, 3 additional toothpicks are added.\n\nLet  $N$  be the number of toothpicks at the 250th stage.\n\nWe first notice that  $N$  is of the form:\n\n\\[ N = 4 + 3(x) \\] where  $x$  represents the number of 3-picks added.\n\nFrom this information, we set  $N$ as follows,\n\n\\[ N = 4 + 3(x) \\]\n\nWe know that 250 is our particular term. Substituting into our formula above, we have:\n\n\\[ 250 = 4 + 3(x) \\]\n\nWe can now solve for  $x$ . \n\nFirst, we move the 4 to the other side by subtracting 4 from each side:\n\n\\[ 250 - 4 = 3x \\]\n\nThen, our equation now reads:\n\n\\[ 246 = 3x \\]\n\nTo solve for  $x$ , we divide both sides by 3:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{246}{3} \\]\n\nWe subtract 4 from both sides again to isolate  $x$ :\n\n\\[\n\\frac{246}{3} - 4 = 82\n\\]\n\nHence, a 250th stage given in the pattern uses 82 3-toothpicks, perfect!\n\nTo summarize, our answer is $\\boxed{82}$. The answer is 82",
